---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import drGreg from "../images/greg-harmeling.jpg";
---

<Layout
	page="about"
	title="About Fenix Therapeutic Services and Gregory Harmeling, Psy.D. "
	description="Read more about Gregory Harmeling, Psy.D, his credentials, and why he might be the right fit to help you on your mental health journey."
>
	<main class="wrapper">
		<section>
			<article>
				<h1>About Fenix Therapeutic Services</h1>

				<Image src={drGreg} alt="Gregory Harmeling, Psy.D." />
				<p>
					Fenix Therapeutic Services is the fully online practice of Dr. Gregory
					Harmeling, Psy.D., a Licensed Marriage and Family Therapist and sex
					therapist with more than twenty years of experience. Greg works with
					people who are rebuilding after relationships that left them doubting
					themselves, especially men who have been through narcissistic,
					psychopathic, or emotionally abusive relationships and aren’t sure
					where to start.
				</p>
				<p>
					His work focuses on trauma, PTSD, men’s issues, recovery from
					narcissistic abuse, and sexual health and intimacy. Many of his
					clients find that healing from an abusive relationship also means
					relearning how to trust, connect, and feel close to someone again, so
					he treats those pieces together rather than separately.
				</p>
				<p>
					Greg is a Certified Clinical Trauma Professional (Level 2), a
					Narcissistic Abuse Treatment Clinician (NATC), and holds a sex therapy
					certification through the Sexual Health Alliance. His approach is
					eclectic and collaborative: rather than fitting clients into one
					method, he works alongside them, drawing on Cognitive Behavioral
					Therapy, Solution-Focused Therapy, and trauma-informed care to build a
					plan that fits their goals and pace.
				</p>
				<p>
					Over his career he has worked with children in foster care, teens in
					the juvenile justice system, adults who have been justice impacted,
					and many adolescents and adults dealing with depression and anxiety.
					That range has taught him to meet people where they are, no matter
					what brought them in.
				</p>
				<p>
					Outside the therapy room, Greg writes about narcissistic abuse
					recovery and relationships on his Substack and shares practical videos
					for survivors on his YouTube channel. Both are free and a good way to
					get a feel for his approach before booking a session.
				</p>
				<p>
					Sessions are held online, so that you can meet with Greg from home, on
					your schedule.
				</p>
			</article>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>

<style lang="scss">
	section {
		padding: 2rem;
		@media (min-width: 1024px) {
			padding: 10rem 5rem;
		}
		article {
			margin: 0 auto;
			h1 {
				margin-bottom: 2rem;
			}
			img {
				border: 2px solid #fff;
				box-shadow: 0 10px 6px -6px #666;
				width: 100%;
				height: auto;
				margin-bottom: 2rem;
				max-width: 350px;
			}
			p {
				margin-bottom: 2rem;
			}
			@media (min-width: 768px) {
				img {
					float: right;
					max-width: 250px;
					margin-left: 3rem;
				}
			}
			@media (min-width: 1500px) {
				max-width: 60%;
			}
		}
	}
</style>
